[{:db/id -1, :adr/id 2799008112, :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/date "2026-07-18", :adr/status :accepted, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-8112 — Mineral and Stone Processing Plant Operators Plant Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Coverage", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8112], :adr/references [2607121000], :adr/related ["2799007211-cloud-itonami-isco-7211-metal-moulders-coremakers-coverage" "2799009311-cloud-itonami-isco-9311-mining-quarrying-labourers-coverage" "2799008341-cloud-itonami-isco-8341-farm-forestry-plant-operators-coverage"], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-8112, :actor/isco-08 "8112", :actor/name "Mineral and Stone Processing Plant Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice", :actor/domain :manufacturing/mineral-stone-plant-scheduling-logistics-coordination, :actor/governor "MineralPlantCoordGovernor", :actor/wave 3, :actor/robotics? true, :actor/coordination? true, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-safety-concern], :actor/hard-checks [:operator-verified :plant-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:finalize-plant-operation-decision :authorize-plant-operation :proceed-with-plant-operation :declare-plant-safety-cleared :finalize-plant-safety-clearance :override-plant-safety-officer-judgment :override-safety-officer-judgment], :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["finalize the plant-operation decision" "finalize the plant operation decision" "proceed with the plant operation" "authorize the plant operation" "commence the plant operation" "declare the plant safety cleared" "declare plant safety cleared" "declare the plant safety clearance" "finalize the plant safety clearance" "override the plant safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override plant safety officer judgment"], :actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}", :actor/confidence-floor 0.6, :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}", :registry/maturity :implemented, :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8112", :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-8112", :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :test/simulator :mineralplant.actor-test, :test/counts "{:total 23, :assertions 49, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :operator-verification :plant-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation :safety-concern-always-escalates], :adr/body "# ADR 2799008112: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 8112 Mineral and Stone Processing Plant Operators plant scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 8112\n-- Mineral and Stone Processing Plant Operators** only, Wave3\n(production/trades) of the rollout (Wave0/1/2 100% complete, Wave3\nbatches 1-11 already landed: 66 occupations so far, the entire 75xx\ncraft-trades range now complete; this batch begins the 81xx/82xx\nplant-and-machine-operator range).\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"8112\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println\n(kotoba.occupation/get-occupation \\\"8112\\\"))\"` from a checkout with\nthe `kotoba-lang/technology` sibling present at the correct\n`../technology` relative path), and its `:name` read exactly \"Mineral\nand Stone Processing Plant Operators\" -- confirming the premise, no\nmismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with\n`:required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no\n`:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository existed at\n`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8112` (`gh api` 404 confirmed before\nscaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry edit promote the\n`8112` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nMineral and Stone Processing Plant Operators run crushing/grinding/\nscreening plant equipment -- real physical-safety stakes (heavy-\nmachinery hazard: crush/entanglement injury) plus dust exposure. The\ncontrolling constraint for this vertical is that the closed op\nallowlist must NEVER include any op that directly finalizes a\nplant-operation-execution decision or a plant-safety-clearance\ndecision, nor override a plant safety officer's judgment -- those\ndecisions must always be a hard permanent block, never\nauto-commit-eligible. This actor is deliberately scoped to PLANT\nSCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION ONLY -- it never operates plant\nequipment or makes safety-clearance decisions itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7211`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7211)\n(Metal Moulders and Coremakers: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor`\nsplit, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set, same heavy-\nmachinery + hazardous-material industrial-site scheduling/logistics\ncoordination shape) -- cloned and read in full in this session. (The\ntask's designated closest-related reference,\n`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8111`, Miners and Quarriers, had not\nyet been merged by any concurrent sibling agent at the time this\nsession began -- confirmed via `gh api` 404 -- so this session fell\nback to `cloud-itonami-isco-7211` per the task's explicit fallback\ninstruction.)\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8112` as an OSS plant\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for mineral and stone\nprocessing plant operators, following the SAME governed-actor\narchitecture as every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this\nfleet: **Mineral and Stone Processing Plant Coordination Advisor ⊣\nMineralPlantCoordGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph\n(`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned identically to the\nreference's `deps.edn` -- a different library coordinate from the\n`langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated `20-actors/*` actor family),\nwith an independent Governor, human-in-the-loop approval via\n`interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **plant scheduling/logistics coordination\nONLY, never direct plant-operation-execution or safety-clearance\nauthority** -- it must NEVER be designed to exercise, simulate\nexercising, or propose exercising a plant-operation-execution\ndecision, a plant-safety-clearance decision, or any override of a\nplant safety officer's judgment. These are not merely gated behind\nescalation -- they are structurally absent from the op-allowlist\nentirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- production-run/inventory/progress data\n  logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/shift/task scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a machinery-hazard/dust-exposure/\n  equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit\n  eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- raw-material/spare-parts procurement\n  proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\nplant-operation-execution decision or a plant-safety-clearance\ndecision, nor an override of a plant safety officer's judgment. These\nare **structurally absent from the op-allowlist entirely**, not merely\ngated behind escalation -- an op such as\n`:finalize-plant-operation-decision` cannot even be proposed by the\nreference mock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for` functions only\never emit one of the four allowlist ops), and if any code path (a\nforged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever\nproduced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD check\n(`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently. A second,\nindependent HARD check (`:scope-excluded-action`) names seven\nconcretely-forbidden ops\n(`mineralplant.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-plant-operation-decision`, `:authorize-plant-operation`,\n`:proceed-with-plant-operation`, `:declare-plant-safety-cleared`,\n`:finalize-plant-safety-clearance`,\n`:override-plant-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`mineralplant.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-plant-operation-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-plant-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-plant-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-plant-safety-cleared`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-plant-safety-officer-judgment`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Operator unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered plant-equipment-operator record\n   (`:no-operator`). Never trusts the proposal's own claim of who the\n   operator is.\n2. **Plant unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an independently\n   registered plant site (`:no-plant`). Together with check 1, this\n   directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that an operator/plant\n   record must be independently verified/registered before any\n   action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the seven\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for a plant-operation-\n   execution decision, a plant-safety-clearance decision, or an\n   override of a plant safety officer's judgment, is a second HARD,\n   PERMANENT block (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated\n   unconditionally on content -- defense-in-depth on top of the\n   allowlist check: even if a future change somehow widened the\n   allowlist, content-based rejection still independently blocks\n   plant-operation-execution/safety-clearance/safety-officer-override\n   language wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a machinery-hazard/\n  dust-exposure/equipment-condition observation -- it never resolves\n  the concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is the hazard\n  data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about plant safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-threshold\n  raw-material/spare-parts order is not itself unsafe, unlike a\n  plant-operation-execution or safety-clearance/safety-officer-\n  override attempt, which is why it is handled by a different\n  mechanism (soft escalate vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"crusher\", \"dust\", \"grinding\") can accidentally match inside the mock\nadvisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly the risk\nthis vertical's own vocabulary (a plant coordination actor working\nadjacent to crushing/grinding/screening equipment necessarily\ndiscusses those concepts to do its scheduling/logging job) could\ntrigger if phrased carelessly.\n`mineralplant.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased exclusively\nas finalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"finalize the plant-operation\ndecision\", \"declare the plant safety cleared\", \"override the plant\nsafety officer's judgment\" -- matching the task's own worked example\nphrasing), never bare nouns, and\n`mineralplant.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for operator ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for\ncrushing/screening shift ...\", \"... routed for plant safety officer\nreview\") WITHOUT containing any of the full finalization-action\nphrases, so the regression test is a genuine stress test of the\nbare-noun-vs-action-phrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on\nfirst run in this session -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard\nitself was never tripped during development.\n`mineralplant.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nadditionally exercises the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"8112\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8112` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-8112`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 23 tests, 49 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy). This actor's test suite has 2 more tests\n  than the mirrored `cloud-itonami-isco-7211` reference (21 tests / 45\n  assertions) because it adds two extra scope-exclusion tests\n  (`hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-plant-safety-cleared` and\n  `hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-declare-plant-safety-cleared`)\n  covering the plant-safety-clearance-decision exclusion, which is a\n  distinct forbidden decision class from the plant-operation-execution\n  exclusion in this vertical's task-specified scope.\n- Ad hoc `clj-kondo` lint of `src`/`test` (this actor's `deps.edn` does\n  not define a `:lint` alias, matching the verified\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7211` reference's own drift, independently\n  confirmed during this session): 1 pre-existing `Unresolved symbol:\n  read-string` error in `mineralplant.advisor`'s `llm-advisor` (the\n  alternate real-LLM advisor swap point, not exercised by the\n  mock-advisor test suite) plus 1 unused-binding warning -- the same\n  lint signature class clj-kondo reports against the mirrored\n  reference repository itself, so this is a pre-existing clj-kondo\n  `.cljc` cross-platform quirk inherited from the mirrored reference,\n  not a regression introduced by this actor.\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-plant-operation` or\n  `:approve-plant-safety-clearance` that is merely gated behind an\n  always-escalate list (the shape `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for\n  `:approve-over-ceiling-posting`): rejected outright per the task's\n  explicit domain-design guidance and the `ADR-2607152500` precedent\n  -- an always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize a\n  plant-operation-execution decision or a plant-safety-clearance\n  decision exists in the code path and is merely deferred to a human\n  gate. For a decision this severe (heavy-machinery crush/entanglement\n  hazard, dust exposure), the capability itself must not exist. The\n  only op related to plant-safety escalation is `:flag-safety-concern`,\n  which surfaces the need for human/plant-safety-officer attention and\n  never itself decides, authorizes, or defers a plant-operation or\n  safety-clearance decision for later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the 3313\n  reference's transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check): rejected per the\n  task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold raw-material/\n  spare-parts order is not itself unsafe, so it is handled as a soft\n  escalate gate, not a hard block; only the\n  plant-operation-execution/plant-safety-clearance/safety-officer-\n  override class is a hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"crusher\" \"dust\"\n  \"grinding\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked example for this\n  exact task, which explicitly warns against exactly this pattern),\n  and per the explicit instruction to phrase scope-exclusion terms as\n  finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare nouns -- this actor's own\n  domain necessarily discusses crusher/dust/grinding concepts to do\n  its scheduling/logging job, so a bare-noun list would risk\n  self-blocking the actor's own legitimate proposals\n  (regression-tested directly against rationale text that deliberately\n  contains those bare nouns).\n- Collapsing the plant-operation-execution exclusion and the\n  plant-safety-clearance exclusion into a single generic\n  \"operational-decision\" exclusion category: rejected -- the task's\n  domain design names these as two textually distinct forbidden\n  decision classes (\"finalize the plant-operation decision\" vs.\n  \"declare the plant safety cleared\"), so this ADR keeps them as\n  separate concretely-named ops and separate scope-excluded phrase\n  entries (with dedicated tests for each) rather than merging them,\n  matching the task's explicit worked phrasing examples verbatim.\n- Merging `operator` and `plant` into a single entity (only checking\n  one provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered operator AND independently-registered\n  plant) matches the CRITICAL invariant that an \"operator/plant record\n  must be independently verified/registered before any action\" and\n  the established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors\n  with two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- production-run/inventory/progress data\n   logging only. Requires an independently registered operator AND\n   plant (`:no-operator`/`:no-plant`). Not a plant-operation-execution\n   or plant-safety-clearance decision in any respect -- it is a\n   records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/shift/task scheduling\n   proposal only. Cannot carry a plant-operation-execution decision\n   (structurally absent from the op's field shape; any such attempt\n   via free text is caught by the `:scope-excluded-action` content\n   check). Does not authorize, finalize, or draw any conclusion about\n   a specific plant operation -- it is a calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a machinery-hazard/dust-\n   exposure/equipment-condition concern to a human/plant safety\n   officer; ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence\n   level, NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through\n   which a safety observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself, nor does it ever\n   declare a plant safety clearance -- the plant safety officer\n   reviews and acts entirely on their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- raw-material/spare-parts\n   procurement proposal only (item, cost). Not a plant-operation-\n   execution or plant-safety-clearance decision of any kind -- it is a\n   purchasing-logistics action, gated by ordinary cost-ceiling\n   escalation (above 2000 always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\ndirectly finalizing a plant-operation-execution decision or a\nplant-safety-clearance decision, nor overriding a plant safety\nofficer's judgment -- these categories are structurally absent, not\ngated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op allowlist itself\n(`mineralplant.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) seven concretely-named\nforbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit level\n(`mineralplant.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`mineralplant.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-plant-operation-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-plant-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-plant-operation`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-plant-safety-cleared`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-plant-safety-officer-judgment`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`mineralplant.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to finalize a plant-operation decision, declare the\nplant safety cleared, or override a plant safety officer's judgment\neven via an otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`mineralplant.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-plant-safety-officer`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-declare-plant-safety-cleared`).\n"}]
